WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.960
In this last video: what the site does on its own, what to do when something goes wrong, and how to clean up after practising.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.509
Some parts of the site update themselves.

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:22.940
Every day, at about half past nine in the morning, new posts from CCS's Spontaneous Order Substack are copied in, and the wiki pages are refreshed.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.855
Neither appears in the CMS.

00:00:24.855 --> 00:00:30.674
In the site's history, these changes appear under the name liberty-lighthouse-bot.

00:00:30.674 --> 00:00:31.880
Leave them alone.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.818
Share cards, site search, and the pages for AI tools rebuild themselves from your content.

00:00:38.818 --> 00:00:44.224
And the three FAQs featured at the top of the homepage aren't set in the CMS.

00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:46.260
To change them, ask Thothica.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:52.016
If your change isn't on the site, wait two to three minutes, then refresh.

00:00:52.016 --> 00:00:55.059
On a phone, close the tab and open it again.

00:00:55.059 --> 00:00:56.718
Check that Draft is off.

00:00:56.718 --> 00:01:03.770
If nobody's changes are going live, a rebuild has failed, and the site stays on its last good version.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:07.573
The usual cause is two glossary terms sharing an alias.

00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:11.860
Think about what was published just before, and tell Thothica.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.455
If a field won't accept what you typed, read the red message under it.

00:01:17.455 --> 00:01:21.755
If Login with GitHub does nothing, allow pop-ups for the site.

00:01:21.755 --> 00:01:27.443
If you're signed in but can't save, your GitHub account may not have write access.

00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:35.280
And if two people edit the same entry, the second save can fail, or overwrite the first, so agree who edits what.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.937
If the site's address doesn't load, use liberty-lighthouse.vercel.app, and tell Thothica.

00:01:41.937 --> 00:01:48.407
If you delete something by mistake, tell Thothica straight away, with its title and roughly when.

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:52.677
Every change is kept in GitHub's history, so it can be restored.

00:01:52.677 --> 00:01:58.280
For anything else, send Thothica the page's address, what you did, and a screenshot.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:05.157
The best way to learn the CMS is to repeat these videos with your own practice entries.

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:08.810
Start each title with Practice, and keep Draft on.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:15.240
Afterwards, type Practice into the search box, and choose All Collections from the menu.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:20.262
Your practice entries are the ones whose titles start with Practice.

00:02:20.262 --> 00:02:25.118
Entries that only mention the word, like the content guide, are not yours.

00:02:25.118 --> 00:02:25.840
Leave them.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.878
Open each one, click Delete entry, and click OK.

00:02:31.878 --> 00:02:34.520
First, the practice video.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.500
Then the practice glossary term.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.400
And the practice comment.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:50.980
Delete a practice topic last, after the practice FAQs and videos in it.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.065
Search all collections again.

00:02:54.065 --> 00:02:58.142
No title starts with Practice now, so you're done.

00:02:58.142 --> 00:03:02.300
Last of all, delete any practice images from Media.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.151
That's everything.

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:14.169
Every step in these videos is also written up in the Editor's Handbook, which you can open from the top bar of the CMS, next to these videos.

00:03:14.169 --> 00:03:15.640
Thank you for watching.
